<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="64.2" level="1">Wills, Trusts, and Fiduciaries</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="III" level="2">Trusts</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="7" level="3">Uniform Trust Code</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="9" level="4">Uniform Prudent Investor Act</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>64.2-787</section_number>
	<catch_line>Reviewing compliance</catch_line>
	<text>
		Compliance with the prudent investor rule is determined in light of the facts and circumstances existing at the time of a trustee's decision or action and not by hindsight.
	</text>
	<history>1999, c. 772, § 26-45.9; 2012, c. 614.</history>
</law>
